--- reason  o1=ok tok=122  o2=ok tok=127  identical=False
o1: Let the cost of the ball be \( b \) dollars.   / The bat costs \( b + 1.00 \) dollars.   /  / Total cost:   / \[ / b + (b + 1.00) = 1.10 / \] /  / Combine terms:   / \[ / 2b + 1.00 = 1.10 / \] /  / Subtract 1.00 from both sides:   / \[ / 2b = 0.10 / \] /  / Divide by 2:   / \[ / b = 0.05 / \] /  / So the ball costs **$0.05** (5 cents).
o2: Let \( b \) be the cost of the ball and \( B \) be the cost of the bat. /  / We are told: /  / \[ / B + b = 1.10 / \] /  / \[ / B = b + 1.00 / \] /  / Substitute the second equation into the first: /  / \[ / (b + 1.00) + b = 1.10 / \] /  / \[ / 2b + 1.00 = 1.10 / \] /  / \[ / 2b = 0.10 / \] /  / \[ / b = 0.05 / \] /  / So the ball costs **$0.05** (5 cents).
